                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "MYTH: The House-passed budget reconciliation package doesn\u2019t do enough to cut spending.\n\nFACT: This is a reconciliation bill, not an appropriations bill. A reconciliation bill can only be used to make changes to certain mandatory spending programs, such as Medicare and Medicaid. An appropriations, or discretionary bill, is what funds government operations on an annual basis. #MythBuster",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1749258211,
                "view_count": 573
